  "response_text": "If we didn\u2019t set the PSP address using the __set_PSP function, the processor would assume that PSP was already pointing to a valid stack with the register values for a thread. However, since PSP was not initialized to anything, it would actually point to a garbage address, and thus the processor would not be able to pop the register values needed to resume thread execution, triggering a hard fault. Calling __set_PSP ensures that the PSP points to a valid address that the processor can resume the thread from.\\n",
